</dir>
<dir path="asciidoctor-pdf/data" level="1">
<abstract>Runtime data shipped with the gem; here only the built-in theme YAML files (the bundled fonts are not included).</abstract>
</dir>
<dir path="asciidoctor-pdf/data/themes" level="2">
<abstract>Built-in themes: base (minimal, PDF standard fonts Helvetica/Courier), default (standalone, Noto Serif and M+ 1mn), default-sans, for-print variants (extend default with black text, grey borders and uncolored links/code) and variants with fallback fonts for CJK/emoji. The default theme lists the default value of almost every theme key.</abstract>
<entry name="base-theme.yml" start="3754" lines="108">Flat-key minimal base theme (page size A4, margins, base settings) that serves as the foundation other themes build on.</entry>
<entry name="default-for-print-theme.yml" start="3864" lines="24">Print-oriented variant extending default that uses black text, grey borders and no link or codespan colors.</entry>
<entry name="default-for-print-with-fallback-font-theme.yml" start="3890" lines="2">Deprecated alias that extends default-for-print-with-font-fallbacks.</entry>
<entry name="default-for-print-with-font-fallbacks-theme.yml" start="3894" lines="3">Combines default-with-font-fallbacks and default-for-print to get the print look with fallback fonts.</entry>
<entry name="default-sans-theme.yml" start="3899" lines="10">Extends default to use the bundled Noto Sans font family for sans-serif body text.</entry>
<entry name="default-sans-with-font-fallbacks-theme.yml" start="3911" lines="3">Combines default-with-font-fallbacks and default-sans for sans text plus fallback fonts.</entry>
<entry name="default-theme.yml" start="3916" lines="261">The built-in default theme defining the font catalog (Noto Serif, M+ 1mn, icon fonts) and styling for every block, heading, table, admonition, header/footer and TOC.</entry>
<entry name="default-with-fallback-font-theme.yml" start="4179" lines="2">Deprecated alias that extends default-with-font-fallbacks.</entry>
<entry name="default-with-font-fallbacks-theme.yml" start="4183" lines="9">Extends default and merges in the M+ 1p Fallback and Noto Emoji fonts as fallbacks for CJK, symbols and emoji.</entry>
</dir>
<dir path="asciidoctor-pdf/docs" level="1">
<abstract>Antora documentation of Asciidoctor PDF: user guide, theming guide (every theme category and key) and extension guide with converter examples, plus the legacy single-page theming-guide stub.</abstract>
<entry name="antora.yml" start="4194" lines="22">Antora component descriptor for the documentation (component name, version 3.0 prerelease, shared AsciiDoc attributes such as url-* links, and the nav file list of the ROOT, theme and extend modules).</entry>
<entry name="theming-guide.adoc" start="4218" lines="8">Stub page stating that the theming guide moved to docs.asciidoctor.org and was split into a Theming section and a Theme Keys Reference.</entry>
</dir>
<dir path="asciidoctor-pdf/docs/modules" level="2">
<abstract>The three Antora modules: ROOT (user guide), theme (theming guide) and extend (extending the converter).</abstract>
</dir>
<dir path="asciidoctor-pdf/docs/modules/extend" level="3">
<abstract>Extension guide: how to subclass and register a custom PDF converter, plus many ready-made Ruby converter extensions for use cases such as custom title/chapter/part pages, chapter TOCs, change bars, table roles, large tables, numbered paragraphs, source language labels and inline page-number macros.</abstract>
<entry name="nav.adoc" start="4228" lines="4">Navigation list of the extend module pages (create converter, use converter, use cases).</entry>
</dir>
<dir path="asciidoctor-pdf/docs/modules/extend/examples" level="4">
<entry name="advanced-inline-pagenum-macro.rb" start="4234" lines="30">Extension example of an inline pagenum macro that can return the page number relative to the document or enclosing section (scope argument), accounting for nested documents and the first page number offset via the pdf-page-start attribute.</entry>
<entry name="breakable-tables-tree-processor.rb" start="4266" lines="12">Tree processor extension that sets the breakable option on every table not already marked breakable or unbreakable, making tables breakable by default.</entry>
<entry name="extended-pdf-converter.rb" start="4280" lines="5">Minimal skeleton of a custom converter class extending the PDF converter (ExtendedPDFConverter) to build on.</entry>
