<entry name="menu.adoc" start="14145" lines="48">Theme keys of the menu category for the inline menu macro.</entry>
<entry name="page-numbers.adoc" start="14195" lines="179">Configuring page numbers: hiding, starting integer numbering, styling and displaying them in running content.</entry>
<entry name="page.adoc" start="14376" lines="200">Theme keys of the page category: size, layout, margins (incl. inner/outer and rotated), columns, background color and page-numbering.</entry>
<entry name="prepare-custom-font.adoc" start="14578" lines="127">Preparing a custom font with a font tool (FontForge): fixing metrics, scripting modifications and required characters.</entry>
<entry name="print-and-prepress.adoc" start="14707" lines="89">Print and prepress media modes (media attribute): double-sided margins and automatic facing pages.</entry>
<entry name="prose.adoc" start="14798" lines="55">Theme keys of the prose category: margin-top/bottom/inner and text-indent for paragraphs.</entry>
<entry name="quote.adoc" start="14855" lines="169">Theme keys of the quote category for quote blocks, including border and quote-cite styling.</entry>
<entry name="quoted-string.adoc" start="15026" lines="26">How content keys accept quoted strings, with escaping rules.</entry>
<entry name="quotes.adoc" start="15054" lines="21">Theme keys of the quotes category for the quotation marks used in text.</entry>
<entry name="role.adoc" start="15077" lines="191">Theme keys of the role category defining built-in and custom roles (font, color, background, border).</entry>
<entry name="running-content.adoc" start="15270" lines="554">Theme keys of the header, footer and running-content categories: height, padding, columns, sectlevels, side/position content, borders and start-at.</entry>
<entry name="section.adoc" start="15826" lines="22">Theme key of the section category (indent for section content).</entry>
<entry name="sidebar.adoc" start="15850" lines="164">Theme keys of the sidebar category for sidebar blocks and sidebar-title.</entry>
<entry name="source-highlighting-theme.adoc" start="16016" lines="94">Selecting a bundled source highlighting theme or defining a custom one.</entry>
<entry name="svg.adoc" start="16112" lines="23">Theme key for SVG images (fonts/generic family mapping used when rendering SVG text).</entry>
<entry name="table.adoc" start="16137" lines="436">Theme keys of the table category: head, body, foot, cell, asciidoc-cell, header-cell, caption, borders, grid and stripes.</entry>
<entry name="tables.adoc" start="16575" lines="215">Table styling topics: border color/style, header bottom border, grid width/color/style, stripe color and caption alignment.</entry>
<entry name="text.adoc" start="16792" lines="195">Text styling properties: decoration, font size, line height, style, transform, superscript, and border/background color.</entry>
<entry name="thematic-break.adoc" start="16989" lines="39">Theme keys of the thematic-break category for horizontal rules.</entry>
<entry name="title-page.adoc" start="17030" lines="535">Theme keys of the title-page category: logo, title, subtitle, authors, revision, background and positions of each element.</entry>
<entry name="title-pages.adoc" start="17567" lines="72">Title page theming topics: background color, background image and logo image.</entry>
<entry name="toc.adoc" start="17641" lines="299">Theme keys of the toc category: toc-h<n> levels, toc-title, dot leader, indent, columns and fonts.</entry>
<entry name="variables.adoc" start="17942" lines="84">Using variables in theme values: referencing keys, math expressions and custom variables.</entry>
<entry name="verse.adoc" start="18028" lines="175">Theme keys of the verse category for verse blocks, incl. border and verse-cite.</entry>
</dir>
<dir path="asciidoctor-pdf/examples" level="1">
<abstract>Sample documents and custom themes (chronicles light/dark) that demonstrate theming and common features; edge-cases.adoc collects tricky inline and block constructs.</abstract>
<entry name="basic-example.adoc" start="18205" lines="39">Small sample AsciiDoc document (TOC, source highlighting, basic blocks) used to demonstrate and generate an example PDF.</entry>
<entry name="chronicles-dark-theme.yml" start="18246" lines="69">Dark-background theme extending chronicles with light text and custom link, codespan and mark colors, for use with the molokai rouge style.</entry>
<entry name="chronicles-example.adoc" start="18317" lines="516">Large showcase book document exercising most features (title page, preface, TOC, index, admonitions, tables, images, source code) for the chronicles theme.</entry>
<entry name="chronicles-theme.yml" start="18835" lines="36">Example custom theme extending default, showing custom roles, abstract, headings, title page, running content and other theme overrides.</entry>
<entry name="edge-cases.adoc" start="18873" lines="78">Book-style document with pagination edge cases such as long listings and blocks that span pages.</entry>
<entry name="sample-banner.svg" start="18953" lines="49">Sample banner SVG logo graphic used by the examples.</entry>
</dir>
<dir path="asciidoctor-pdf/lib" level="1">
<abstract>Ruby source of the gem: entry points that register the converter and the asciidoctor/pdf namespace with the converter, theme loader, inline formatting, measurement helpers, optimizers and Prawn extensions.</abstract>
<entry name="asciidoctor-pdf.rb" start="19004" lines="3">Gem entry point that just requires the main library so `require 'asciidoctor-pdf'` loads the converter.</entry>
</dir>
<dir path="asciidoctor-pdf/lib/asciidoctor" level="2">
<abstract>Namespace directory containing the Asciidoctor PDF library: the main loader file and the pdf/ implementation directory.</abstract>
<entry name="pdf.rb" start="19009" lines="20">Library bootstrap that loads Asciidoctor, Prawn and prawn-templates and then requires the measurements, sanitizer, text transformer, extension patches, theme loader and converter in dependency order.</entry>
</dir>
<dir path="asciidoctor-pdf/lib/asciidoctor/pdf" level="3">
<abstract>Implementation: the converter (all node conversions and page layout), theme loader and theme data, inline formatted-text parser and transforms, sanitizer, measurement and roman numeral helpers, index catalog, section-by-page tracking, pdfmark writer, PDF optimizers (rghost/hexapdf), image-format fallbacks, and patches to Prawn, prawn-table, prawn-svg, prawn-icon, Rouge and Ruby core classes.</abstract>
<entry name="converter.rb" start="19031" lines="5464">The PDF converter (a Prawn::Document subclass) that implements every AsciiDoc node conversion: document setup (theme loading, page size/margins/layout, fonts, running content, front/back cover, title page, TOC, index, outline/bookmarks, PDF metadata, page numbering, columns), sections/parts/chapters/floating titles/preamble/abstract/index sections, paragraphs, admonitions (icons/labels), listing/literal/source code (Rouge/Pygments/CodeRay highlighting, callouts, line numbers, tab expansion, linenum/highlight lines), collapsible/example/open/quote/verse/sidebar blocks, ordered/unordered/description/callout/horizontal/checklist lists and list item markers, block and inline images (scaling, fit, align, float, pdfwidth/scaledwidth, SVG, caption, link, image format and fallback), audio/video placeholders, page breaks, passthrough, stem, tables (cell styles, spans, header/footer rows, widths, AsciiDoc cells, striping, borders, autowidth), thematic breaks, TOC macro, and all inline nodes (anchors/xrefs/links/footnotes, icons, kbd/menu/button, quoted text, index terms, callouts), plus destinations, heading arrangement, discrete subs and keep-together/extent helpers.</entry>
<entry name="ext.rb" start="24497" lines="10">Aggregator that loads all monkey patches for Ruby core, Asciidoctor, pdf-core, Prawn, prawn-gmagick, prawn-icon, prawn-svg and prawn-table.</entry>
<entry name="formatted_string.rb" start="24509" lines="13">A String subclass that carries pre-parsed text fragments alongside the plain text so formatted content survives being passed as a string, with equality that also compares fragments.</entry>
<entry name="formatted_text.rb" start="24524" lines="13">Aggregator that requires the Treetop markup parser, transform, formatter and the fragment render-behind callbacks (destination marker, inline image, text aligner, background/border, source wrap) used for inline formatted text.</entry>
<entry name="index_catalog.rb" start="24539" lines="208">Collects index terms (primary/secondary/tertiary, categorized by first letter and sorted by locale) with their destinations and see/see-also associations, and resolves each term's destinations to physical page numbers for the generated index.</entry>
<entry name="measurements.rb" start="24749" lines="62">Converts measurement strings with units (pt, in, cm, mm, px, em/rem, percent) into points, including multi-value strings, as used for theme values and block attributes such as pdfwidth.</entry>
<entry name="nogmagick.rb" start="24813" lines="6">Opt-out shim that unregisters the GMagick image handler and restores Prawn's built-in PNG handler so GraphicsMagick is not used at all.</entry>
<entry name="nopngmagick.rb" start="24821" lines="3">Opt-out shim that re-registers Prawn's native PNG handler so GMagick is used for other formats but not for PNG.</entry>
<entry name="optimizer.rb" start="24826" lines="56">Defines the pluggable PDF optimizer interface (quality, compatibility level, PDF/A-style compliance options) and the registry/factory that resolves an optimizer by name, lazily loading the rghost one.</entry>
<entry name="pdfmark.rb" start="24884" lines="48">Generates the pdfmark file used by optimizers to preserve document info (title, author(s), subject, keywords, publisher, creation/mod dates, reproducible mode, untitled-label fallback).</entry>
<entry name="roman_numeral.rb" start="24934" lines="110">Roman numeral value object (upper/lower case) with succ/pred and integer conversion, used for front-matter page numbering such as the roman numerals in the table of contents pages.</entry>
<entry name="sanitizer.rb" start="25046" lines="54">Helpers to strip inline XML tags, resolve named/numeric character references (with a fallback for unknown entities) and escape/unescape XML special characters or bare ampersands in strings.</entry>
<entry name="section_info_by_page.rb" start="25102" lines="24">Per-page lookup table recording the section title and numeral that applies to each page, used for running header/footer content such as section-title and chapter-title.</entry>
<entry name="text_transformer.rb" start="25128" lines="106">Applies the theme text-transform values (uppercase, lowercase, capitalize, smallcaps) and hyphenation to text while leaving markup tags untouched.</entry>
<entry name="theme_data.rb" start="25236" lines="57">Struct-like container for theme settings that exposes keys as methods with symbol-normalized keys, returning nil for missing keys, and supports dup/merge-style access.</entry>
<entry name="theme_loader.rb" start="25295" lines="323">Loads and parses YAML theme files (default/base theme resolution, extends inheritance, theme and font asset directory lookup), normalizes keys (dashes, prefixes like base/heading), and evaluates values: hex/RGB/CMYK/transparent colors, variable references, math expressions and units.</entry>
<entry name="version.rb" start="25620" lines="7">Defines the gem version constant.</entry>
</dir>
<dir path="asciidoctor-pdf/lib/asciidoctor/pdf/ext" level="4">
<entry name="asciidoctor.rb" start="25629" lines="8">Aggregator that loads the patches to Asciidoctor core classes (abstract block, document, section, list, image).</entry>
<entry name="core.rb" start="25639" lines="6">Aggregator that loads the patches to Ruby core classes (File, Object, String) and the stdout wrapper.</entry>
<entry name="pdf-core.rb" start="25647" lines="3">Aggregator that loads the pdf-core page patch.</entry>
<entry name="prawn-gmagick.rb" start="25652" lines="18">Optionally loads prawn-gmagick and patches it to read the correct bit depth of PNG images (works around a known prawn-gmagick bug).</entry>
<entry name="prawn-icon.rb" start="25672" lines="20">Patches prawn-icon to reuse an icon font already registered in the document's font catalog, silence its compatibility warnings, and loads the legacy/interface extensions.</entry>
<entry name="prawn-svg.rb" start="25694" lines="18">Loads prawn-svg (suppressing its experimental-feature warning on old Rubies), pulls in the SVG patches, and clears system font paths so SVG text rendering is portable.</entry>
<entry name="prawn-table.rb" start="25714" lines="17">Patches prawn-table so a table whose header rows do not fit on the remaining page moves to a new page, and loads the cell overrides.</entry>
<entry name="prawn.rb" start="25733" lines="19">Adjusts Prawn's float precision constant (needed for column spans in tables) and loads all Prawn patches such as column box, fonts, images, formatted text and extensions.</entry>
<entry name="pygments.rb" start="25754" lines="36">Extracts background, foreground and highlight-line colors from a Pygments style's CSS so source blocks can match the chosen Pygments style, and reports whether a style exists.</entry>
<entry name="rouge.rb" start="25792" lines="4">Aggregator that loads the Rouge Prawn formatter and the default Rouge theme.</entry>
</dir>
<dir path="asciidoctor-pdf/lib/asciidoctor/pdf/ext/asciidoctor" level="5">
<entry name="abstract_block.rb" start="25798" lines="35">Adds tree-navigation helpers to blocks (empty?, first/last child, next/previous sibling, remove) used by the converter when deciding spacing and keep-together behavior.</entry>
<entry name="document.rb" start="25835" lines="47">Backports to Document: promotes a titled preamble in a book to a preface section (including notitle/lead handling) and detects whether an attribute was ever explicitly set, which decides defaults like part/chapter signifiers.</entry>
<entry name="image.rb" start="25884" lines="30">Parses image targets including base64 data URIs (png, jpeg, gif, pdf, bmp, tiff, svg) and derives the image format from the extension or format attribute, with jpg and svg+xml aliases.</entry>
<entry name="list.rb" start="25916" lines="27">Adds nested? and list_level to lists, counting only list ancestors, which drives unordered list marker selection by nesting depth.</entry>
<entry name="section.rb" start="25945" lines="40">Computes section titles with numbering, including book part/chapter signifiers (part-signifier, chapter-signifier), sectnumlevels limits and captioned appendix titles, and detects the first section of a part.</entry>
</dir>
<dir path="asciidoctor-pdf/lib/asciidoctor/pdf/ext/core" level="5">
<entry name="file.rb" start="25987" lines="14">JRuby-only workaround that fixes File.absolute_path and absolute_path? so URLs and relative directory resolution behave correctly.</entry>
<entry name="object.rb" start="26003" lines="8">Adds to_pdf_object to every object to serialize it as a PDF object.</entry>
<entry name="quantifiable_stdout.rb" start="26013" lines="25">STDOUT wrapper that counts bytes written so the size of a PDF streamed to stdout can be reported.</entry>
<entry name="string.rb" start="26040" lines="22">Adds String helpers: pred (previous integer or character used for counting down list numbers), as_pdf and to_pdf_object (ASCII strings become PDF literal strings).</entry>
</dir>
<dir path="asciidoctor-pdf/lib/asciidoctor/pdf/ext/pdf-core" level="5">
<entry name="page.rb" start="26064" lines="37">Extends PDF::Core::Page with tracking of the empty content stream (to detect blank pages), an imported-page flag and reset_content to clear a page.</entry>
</dir>
<dir path="asciidoctor-pdf/lib/asciidoctor/pdf/ext/prawn" level="5">
<entry name="coderay_encoder.rb" start="26103" lines="106">CodeRay encoder that turns tokens into Prawn text fragments with colors/styles from the CodeRay theme, used for syntax highlighting source blocks with CodeRay.</entry>
<entry name="extensions.rb" start="26211" lines="1187">Large Prawn::Document mixin of layout and drawing helpers: page margins/sides (recto/verso), page dimensions, font handling and styles with fallback fonts, formatted text boxes and first-line formatting, cursor movement and float, keep-together extents, padding/indent/rect value expansion, column boxes, fills, horizontal/vertical rules, destinations, page deletion and PDF page import.</entry>
<entry name="font_metric_cache.rb" start="27400" lines="9">Compatibility patch for Prawn's font metric cache entries so cache keys work with fonts (to be removed with prawn 2.5).</entry>
<entry name="images.rb" start="27411" lines="67">Overrides Prawn's image method to cache image info, produce clearer errors for unsupported or corrupt images and recommend prawn-gmagick for interlaced or unsupported PNGs.</entry>
</dir>
<dir path="asciidoctor-pdf/lib/asciidoctor/pdf/ext/prawn/document" level="6">
<entry name="column_box.rb" start="27480" lines="45">Extends Prawn's ColumnBox to track the current column, reflow margins across page breaks with changed margins, preserve indentation, and collapse to a single column for measuring content.</entry>
</dir>
<dir path="asciidoctor-pdf/lib/asciidoctor/pdf/ext/prawn/font" level="6">
<entry name="afm.rb" start="27527" lines="29">Makes built-in (AFM) font text encoding fall back gracefully to Windows-1252 with substitutions for characters like thin space and a warning plus replacement symbol for untranslatable text.</entry>
<entry name="ttf.rb" start="27558" lines="8">Patches TTF character width lookup so code 0 has zero width.</entry>
</dir>
<dir path="asciidoctor-pdf/lib/asciidoctor/pdf/ext/prawn/formatted_text" level="6">
<entry name="arranger.rb" start="27568" lines="61">Patches the text arranger for custom behaviors: skipping left-strip, preview of the joined line string, finalizing lines and applying font size changes with styles to fragments.</entry>
<entry name="box.rb" start="27631" lines="119">Patches the formatted text box with fragment overlay styles (background, border, underline, etc.), fallback-font glyph selection per character, word spacing for justified lines and vertical alignment of text.</entry>
<entry name="fragment.rb" start="27752" lines="50">Patches text fragments: concealing text while keeping its width, preserving soft hyphens, ascender/descender and explicit width/border-offset overrides from the format state, and zero-width space stripping.</entry>
<entry name="indented_paragraph_wrap.rb" start="27804" lines="39">Adds first-line paragraph indentation (indent_paragraphs) support to the formatted text box wrapping algorithm.</entry>
<entry name="line_wrap.rb" start="27845" lines="42">Overrides line wrapping to add fragments token by token, handle zero-width spaces and soft hyphen width, single-token fragments and newlines, and break long tokens.</entry>
<entry name="protect_bottom_gutter.rb" start="27889" lines="16">Wrap extension that reserves a bottom gutter on the last line of a text block so the final line does not land at the very bottom of a page (unless full_height fragments are present).</entry>
</dir>
<dir path="asciidoctor-pdf/lib/asciidoctor/pdf/ext/prawn-icon" level="5">
<entry name="interface.rb" start="27907" lines="11">Adds icon font data lookup and legacy Font Awesome 4 name resolution (fa-prefixed) to the prawn-icon interface.</entry>
<entry name="legacy.rb" start="27920" lines="11">Loads the YAML mapping from legacy Font Awesome 4 icon names to current Font Awesome icon names.</entry>
</dir>
<dir path="asciidoctor-pdf/lib/asciidoctor/pdf/ext/prawn-svg" level="5">
<entry name="url_loader.rb" start="27933" lines="13">Reconfigures prawn-svg's URL loader so data URIs, web (http/https) and file loaders can be individually enabled, with file access restricted to a root.</entry>
</dir>
<dir path="asciidoctor-pdf/lib/asciidoctor/pdf/ext/prawn-svg/calculators" level="6">
<entry name="document_sizing.rb" start="27948" lines="9">Converts px-valued SVG width/height to points (0.75 factor) when sizing an SVG document.</entry>
</dir>
<dir path="asciidoctor-pdf/lib/asciidoctor/pdf/ext/prawn-svg/elements" level="6">
<entry name="image.rb" start="27959" lines="15">Makes SVG image elements get dimensions from Prawn's image handlers and skip unsupported embedded image types with a clear error.</entry>
</dir>
<dir path="asciidoctor-pdf/lib/asciidoctor/pdf/ext/prawn-svg/loaders" level="6">
<entry name="data.rb" start="27976" lines="6">Restricts the SVG data URI loader to base64-encoded png, jpeg and svg images.</entry>
<entry name="file.rb" start="27984" lines="22">Adds a jail path to the SVG file loader so referenced files outside the permitted root (e.g. with allow-uri-read or safe mode) are rejected.</entry>
<entry name="web.rb" start="28008" lines="22">SVG web loader that fetches only http/https URLs via open-uri (lazily loaded or injected via proc) and wraps failures in loader errors.</entry>
</dir>
<dir path="asciidoctor-pdf/lib/asciidoctor/pdf/ext/prawn-table" level="5">
<entry name="cell.rb" start="28032" lines="68">Patches prawn-table cell border color handling and border drawing (per-side widths/colors/styles).</entry>
</dir>
<dir path="asciidoctor-pdf/lib/asciidoctor/pdf/ext/prawn-table/cell" level="6">
<entry name="asciidoc.rb" start="28102" lines="133">Custom table cell type for AsciiDoc-style (a) cells that renders nested blocks via the converter, measuring natural width/height in a scratch dry run and applying inherited font properties.</entry>
<entry name="text.rb" start="28237" lines="54">Overrides text cell drawing and width calculation: accounts for inline image widths and hard line breaks, vertical centering, and logs an error when cell content exceeds the height of a single page (truncated).</entry>
</dir>
<dir path="asciidoctor-pdf/lib/asciidoctor/pdf/ext/rouge" level="5">
</dir>
<dir path="asciidoctor-pdf/lib/asciidoctor/pdf/ext/rouge/formatters" level="6">
<entry name="prawn.rb" start="28293" lines="205">Rouge formatter that converts highlighted tokens into Prawn text fragments (colors, bold/italic, line numbers, highlighted lines with background, per-line fragments) for source blocks highlighted with Rouge.</entry>
</dir>
<dir path="asciidoctor-pdf/lib/asciidoctor/pdf/ext/rouge/themes" level="6">
<entry name="asciidoctor_pdf_default.rb" start="28500" lines="69">Default Rouge color theme for source highlighting (token to color/style mapping) used when no source-highlighter theme is chosen.</entry>
</dir>
<dir path="asciidoctor-pdf/lib/asciidoctor/pdf/formatted_text" level="4">
<entry name="formatter.rb" start="28571" lines="47">Entry point that parses inline HTML-like markup (produced by Asciidoctor's inline conversion) into Prawn fragments, normalizing whitespace and logging parse errors, and treats pre-split paragraphs as a single paragraph.</entry>
<entry name="fragment_position_renderer.rb" start="28620" lines="18">Callback that records a fragment's position (top, left, bottom, right, page) so the converter can later place links, anchors or overlays relative to rendered text.</entry>
<entry name="inline_destination_marker.rb" start="28640" lines="19">Callback that creates a named PDF destination at the precise position of an inline anchor or index term (linking index terms to pages) without printing any text.</entry>
<entry name="inline_image_arranger.rb" start="28661" lines="157">Resolves inline images during text layout: loads raster/SVG images, handles missing or unreadable images with alt-text fallback and warnings, computes width/height (px, pt, percent, fit constraints), and adjusts line height when an image is taller than the text.</entry>
<entry name="inline_image_renderer.rb" start="28820" lines="48">Draws inline images (raster or SVG) at the position reserved in the text line, centered vertically or bottom-aligned when taller than 1.5x the text.</entry>
<entry name="inline_text_aligner.rb" start="28870" lines="25">Callback that draws a text fragment itself with center or right alignment within a fixed width or border offset, used for aligned inline content such as callout numbers or badges.</entry>
<entry name="parser.rb" start="28897" lines="1174">Generated Treetop parser (from a grammar) for the inline markup subset: tags with attributes, void elements, CDATA, and numeric/named character references and spaces.</entry>
<entry name="source_wrap.rb" start="30073" lines="54">Wrap extension for source blocks that prefixes each wrapped line with a spacer matching the line-number width and carries over line highlight so wrapped lines stay aligned with line numbers.</entry>
<entry name="text_background_and_border_renderer.rb" start="30129" lines="51">Callback that paints inline background colors, borders, border radius and block-style inline backgrounds (e.g. for code, mark and kbd spans) behind text fragments.</entry>
<entry name="transform.rb" start="30182" lines="457">Transforms the parsed inline markup tree into Prawn fragment hashes, mapping tags and attributes (b, i, code, mark, kbd, font, span, a, color, link, img, sub/sup, strikethrough, underline, etc.) and theme-driven styles (colors, backgrounds, borders, text transforms) onto formatting properties.</entry>
</dir>
<dir path="asciidoctor-pdf/lib/asciidoctor/pdf/optimizer" level="4">
<entry name="rghost.rb" start="30641" lines="103">Optimizer implementation that shells out to Ghostscript through the RGhost gem to compress/optimize a generated PDF (quality presets, PDF compatibility level, pdfmark, PDF/A-style compliance).</entry>
</dir>
<dir path="asciidoctor-pdf/scripts" level="1">
<abstract>Development helper scripts that switch the Gemfile to the development heads of Asciidoctor or Prawn.</abstract>
<entry name="switch-to-asciidoctor-head.rb" start="30746" lines="14">CI helper that replaces the installed asciidoctor gem with a clone of a given git branch to test against asciidoctor HEAD.</entry>
<entry name="switch-to-prawn-head.rb" start="30762" lines="36">CI helper that replaces the installed prawn gem with a clone of prawn HEAD while patching dependency requirements.</entry>
</dir>
<dir path="asciidoctor-pdf/spec" level="1">
<abstract>RSpec test suite, one file per feature (admonition, table, image, list, section, toc, title page, running content, theme loader, font, xref, ...). Each test shows an AsciiDoc input and the expected PDF output or log message, which makes these files the most precise description of edge-case behavior; plus fixtures and test helpers.</abstract>
<entry name="abstract_spec.rb" start="30800" lines="705">Tests the abstract block: outdent/indent, prose_text_indent(_inner) theme keys, nested non-paragraph blocks, first-line decoration (font color/style, text transform and shrink-to-fit, justification), text alignment of abstract and its title, and use inside column boxes.</entry>
<entry name="admonition_spec.rb" start="31507" lines="1341">Tests admonitions: label text (bold, transform, resize on overflow, min width), icon modes (font/SVG/image via icon attribute or theme, stroke color, remote images with allow-uri-read), background/border/column-rule theme keys, and page-break behavior of split blocks.</entry>
<entry name="api_spec.rb" start="32850" lines="24">Tests the Ruby API, i.e. Asciidoctor.convert and convert_file returning a Prawn::Document instance or writing a PDF file.</entry>
<entry name="arrange_block_spec.rb" start="32876" lines="2121">Tests the arrange_block layout engine for unbreakable and breakable blocks at/below top of page, in table cells and column boxes: dry-run advance vs. split across pages, captions, anchors, images taller than the page, rotated pages, and background extents.</entry>
<entry name="audio_spec.rb" start="34999" lines="58">Tests that an audio block is replaced by a pointer, the path/URL to the audio file, and its title.</entry>
<entry name="break_spec.rb" start="35059" lines="449">Tests line breaks (hard break, [%hardbreaks]), thematic breaks (theme line style/width/spacing), and page breaks (advance page, columns, layout switching mid-document).</entry>
<entry name="cli_spec.rb" start="35510" lines="172">Tests the asciidoctor-pdf command line: version output, options (--theme, -a, -o, -D, stdin/stdout redirection), --require, theme and font dir flags, packaging examples, nogmagick handling, pdfmark generation, and keeping artifacts.</entry>
<entry name="converter_spec.rb" start="35684" lines="1566">Tests converter internals: register_for, convert in secure mode and file output, theme selection (pdf-theme, default-sans), error logging, extending the converter (custom ink methods, layout_heading), and next_enclosed_block helper across sections, lists, abstract, preamble and nested blocks.</entry>
<entry name="cover_page_spec.rb" start="37252" lines="549">Tests front and back cover pages: front-cover-image/cover_back_image theme key, image path resolution, scaling for different aspect ratios, importing a page from a PDF cover, prepress recto margins on the title page, and missing/empty PDF handling.</entry>
<entry name="dest_spec.rb" start="37803" lines="406">Tests named destinations (anchors) registered in the PDF: __anchor-top, section/part page dests, lists with IDs, inline anchors, and auto-generated section ids not being registered.</entry>
<entry name="diagram_spec.rb" start="38211" lines="120">Tests integration with asciidoctor-diagram and asciidoctor-kroki: locating generated diagram images with to_dir/imagesdir and overwriting on repeated invocations.</entry>
<entry name="document_title_spec.rb" start="38333" lines="93">Tests document title handling for book and article doctypes, including partitioning main title and subtitle.</entry>
<entry name="example_spec.rb" start="38428" lines="423">Tests example blocks: keeping the block together on a page, bottom padding at page end, theme border style/colors/background, titles/captions, and collapsible blocks with fallback title.</entry>
<entry name="floating_title_spec.rb" start="38853" lines="345">Tests discrete (floating) headings: heading alignment from theme, heading-min-height-after behavior, not outdenting inside blocks, and level styling.</entry>
<entry name="font_spec.rb" start="39200" lines="564">Tests fonts: bundled default theme fonts and fallback fonts (emoji, notdef), built-in AFM fonts, OTF/TTF custom fonts and font paths/errors, kerning, no-break space and line breaks, separators, and font size resolution (percent, em).</entry>
<entry name="footnote_spec.rb" start="39766" lines="655">Tests footnotes: placement per chapter or document end, footnotes_margin_top, label keeping with preceding text, unresolved references in red, footnotes-title, repeated references, and footnotes inside table cells and horizontal lists.</entry>
<entry name="formatted_text_formatter_spec.rb" start="40423" lines="1334">Tests inline formatting: HTML markup (strong, em, mono, sub/sup, span, font, background/border on phrases), character references, roles (underline, big/small, custom theme roles), typographic quotes, menu/kbd/button, text transform, and fallback-font handling.</entry>
<entry name="formatted_text_spec.rb" start="41759" lines="11">Tests that the formatted text extension does not wrap a LoadError when a require fails.</entry>
<entry name="formatted_text_transform_spec.rb" start="41772" lines="227">Tests the formatted text transform that converts parsed inline HTML into Prawn fragments: strong/em/color fragments, space collapsing around empty elements, hex colors, and nil result for invalid markup.</entry>
<entry name="hyphens_spec.rb" start="42001" lines="239">Tests hyphenation via the hyphens attribute: paragraphs, table cells and heads, language from lang attribute, soft hyphens, and interaction with justification and links.</entry>
<entry name="icon_spec.rb" start="42242" lines="325">Tests inline icons: icon name fallback when font icons are disabled, icon sets as prefix (fas, far, fab), fw sizing, size/rotate/flip attributes, link attribute, and icon theme keys.</entry>
<entry name="ignore-gem-warnings.rb" start="42569" lines="11">Spec helper that overrides Warning#warn to suppress warnings originating from installed gem paths.</entry>
<entry name="image_float_spec.rb" start="42582" lines="985">Tests floated block images (float=left/right): text wrapping in float box, captions, paragraph fitting and advancing, anchors, floats inside delimited blocks, unknown float values, and unfloated paragraphs.</entry>
<entry name="image_spec.rb" start="43569" lines="3125">Tests block and inline images: imagesdir resolution, alignment, width units (pt/px/%/vw), SVG/raster/BMP/GIF/PDF formats, data URIs, remote images and cache, missing images with alt text, captions, borders, links, fit/scaling, and page-break behavior.</entry>
<entry name="index_spec.rb" start="46696" lines="1477">Tests the index: index section generation, entry grouping and sorting (asciibetical, ICU), page number links and ranges, see/see also associations, columns, prepress page numbering, TOC inclusion, and empty index handling.</entry>
<entry name="link_spec.rb" start="48175" lines="376">Tests links: raw URL and email conversion, breaking long bare URLs, showing link URIs for print/prepress media, unknown references, and theme link styling (color, text decoration).</entry>
<entry name="list_spec.rb" start="48553" lines="2339">Tests lists: unordered/ordered (markers by level, styles, start values), checklists, mixed nesting, description lists (term styling, horizontal, Q&A), callout lists, bibliography lists, theme keys for markers/indent/spacing/line height, and page-break behavior.</entry>
<entry name="listing_spec.rb" start="50894" lines="951">Tests listing/literal blocks: empty blocks, unbreakable/breakable_min_lines and code_orphans handling across pages, anchor placement (block_anchor_top), split-block dashed border, line wrapping, autofit with minimum font sizes, nbsp indentation guard, tab expansion (tabsize), listing-caption and caption theme keys (background, below block), conum font/color, per-edge border width and padding theme keys, and callouts substitution.</entry>
<entry name="manpage_spec.rb" start="51847" lines="124">Tests manpage doctype: auto-generated NAME section (substitutions on manname, title uppercasing rules) and arranging the manpage body into columns via theme.</entry>
<entry name="media_spec.rb" start="51973" lines="189">Tests media=print/prepress behavior: default-for-print theme selection, blank pages inserted after image/PDF cover and after TOC, no blank page at start or before chapters following preamble/title, and color space on empty verso pages.</entry>
<entry name="open_spec.rb" start="52164" lines="156">Tests open blocks: breakable by default, unbreakable option (keeps together or breaks if longer than a page), title and keeping title with content on page advance, and avoiding unnecessary dry runs.</entry>
<entry name="optimizer_spec.rb" start="52322" lines="305">Tests PDF optimization via Ghostscript (optimize attribute): quality values and grayscale/bw modifiers, pdf-version and PDF/A or PDF/X compliance, link preservation, filenames with spaces, pdfmark reuse, the asciidoctor-pdf-optimize CLI, GS/GS_OPTIONS environment variables, and custom/registered optimizers.</entry>
<entry name="outline_spec.rb" start="52629" lines="839">Tests the PDF outline (bookmarks): outline attribute, toclevels/outlinelevels depth and expand levels, doctitle entry (outline-title, untitled-label, notitle, cover pages), notitle sections and empty entries, page labels (roman numerals for front matter), and title sanitization.</entry>
<entry name="page_spec.rb" start="53470" lines="1877">Tests page setup: page size (theme page_size, pdf-page-size names/arrays/inches and invalid values), layout, initial zoom, page mode (outline/none/thumbs/fullscreen), margins (theme, pdf-page-margin, rotated pages, prepress recto/verso, folio placement inversion), and multi-column article layout (columns, gap, footnotes, title/TOC outside columns).</entry>
<entry name="paragraph_spec.rb" start="55349" lines="302">Tests paragraphs: whitespace normalization, page-boundary flow, first-line indent (prose_text_indent, prose_text_indent_inner, prose_margin_inner) and alignment exceptions, text-align attribute, block titles and caption alignment, lead role styling, and theme font properties and line height for roles.</entry>
<entry name="pass_spec.rb" start="55653" lines="43">Tests passthrough blocks: rendered as plain literal text and given bottom margin.</entry>
<entry name="pdf_info_spec.rb" start="55698" lines="360">Tests PDF metadata: PDF version/compliance (pdf-version), Creator/Producer/Author/Subject/Keywords from attributes (author, authors, publisher, non-Latin, sanitization), date handling (invalid dates, reproducible, SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH), Title field (untitled-label, formatting removal, hex encoding), and stream compression.</entry>
<entry name="pdfmark_spec.rb" start="56060" lines="224">Tests pdfmark generation: pdfmark info from document attributes (title, untitled-label, author/authors, sanitization, dates, reproducible, SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH) and writing a .pdfmark file when the pdfmark attribute is set, with hex-encoded non-ASCII titles.</entry>
<entry name="preamble_spec.rb" start="56286" lines="267">Tests preamble handling: when the first preamble paragraph is styled as lead (articles vs books, existing role, no sections, abstract), empty preambles, promotion to preface via preface-title, and theme lead style.</entry>
<entry name="quote_spec.rb" start="56555" lines="371">Tests quote blocks: title caption above, attribution and citetitle (ampersand escaping, character references, substitutions), alignment roles, left border rules (width 0/nil, transparent color), background/border colors, padding, borders and caption across page splits, and bottom padding near page end.</entry>
<entry name="running_content_spec.rb" start="56928" lines="3575">Tests running headers and footers: activation, start-at and page numbering (folio, pagenums), theme keys, recto/verso folio placement, page layout (rotated pages), implicit attributes (page-number, section titles, etc.), and images in header/footer content.</entry>
<entry name="section_spec.rb" start="60505" lines="1691">Tests sections: heading styles per level and part/chapter/appendix handling, section numbering and titles, indent (section indent), page breaks around chapters, discrete headings, anchors, and theme heading keys.</entry>
<entry name="sidebar_spec.rb" start="62198" lines="366">Tests sidebar blocks: title, background/border theme keys, padding, content alignment, and page-split behavior.</entry>
<entry name="source_spec.rb" start="62566" lines="1998">Tests source blocks and syntax highlighting with Rouge, CodeRay, and Pygments: lexer fallback, tab expansion, PHP start_inline and CGI-style options, rouge-style themes and token styling (bold/italic/underline/background), linenums with start values and page splits, callouts, and unsupported highlighter handling and labels.</entry>
<entry name="spec_helper.rb" start="64566" lines="37">RSpec helper (not a test): shared setup and utilities such as to_pdf/to_file converters, text/image/line/rect extraction helpers, example group tagging (visual, cli, network), and fixtures used by all specs.</entry>
<entry name="stem_spec.rb" start="64605" lines="65">Tests stem blocks: rendered as code blocks without a stem extension, indentation preserved, and caption plus anchor above the block.</entry>
<entry name="table_spec.rb" start="64672" lines="3755">Tests tables: decoration (borders, grid, stripes), dimensions (column widths, autowidth, width attribute), extent and page splitting, cell styles (basic, strong, monospaced, head/header, foot, literal, verse, AsciiDoc cells), caption, alignment, cell spanning, and arranging blocks around tables.</entry>
<entry name="thematic_break_spec.rb" start="68429" lines="248">Tests thematic breaks: margins and padding (including fallbacks and at top of page), width, border style (solid, dashed, dotted, double), and border color rules (base color fallback, transparent).</entry>
<entry name="theme_loader_spec.rb" start="68679" lines="1463">Tests the theme loader: loading YAML themes, extends resolution, data types (colors, measurements, fonts, math), variable interpolation, theme file/asset path resolution, and error cases.</entry>
<entry name="title_page_spec.rb" start="70144" lines="1416">Tests the title page: book doctype and title-page attribute behavior, document title, author, revision, and subtitle layout, logo image (positioning, scaling), background image/color, and theming keys.</entry>
<entry name="toc_spec.rb" start="71562" lines="1814">Tests the table of contents for books and articles: toc attribute and placement (macro, preamble, auto), toclevels, title and numbering, dot leaders and page numbers, links, indent and theme keys, and page labels.</entry>
<entry name="verse_spec.rb" start="73378" lines="302">Tests verse blocks: title caption, attribution line, tab expansion and indentation, alignment role, left border rules, verse theme category styling, background/border colors, padding, and split-page borders.</entry>
<entry name="video_spec.rb" start="73682" lines="132">Tests video blocks: poster image replacement, fallback to video path with play icon, text wrapping, caption, and local/YouTube/Vimeo behavior depending on the allow-uri-read attribute.</entry>
<entry name="xref_spec.rb" start="73816" lines="492">Tests cross references: internal xrefs to sections/anchors/blocks, interdocument xrefs, xrefstyle (full/short/basic), missing targets, and link output.</entry>
</dir>
<dir path="asciidoctor-pdf/spec/fixtures" level="2">
<abstract>Inputs used by the specs: AsciiDoc documents (book samples, includes, chapters, edge cases), custom theme YAML files, SVG/PNG/JPG/GIF images, an extra font and small helper files.</abstract>
<entry name="admonition-image-theme.yml" start="74310" lines="5">Theme extending default that sets an SVG image as the note admonition icon.</entry>
<entry name="arrange-block-at-top-does-not-fit.adoc" start="74317" lines="1060">Blocks (admonitions, etc.) placed at the top of a page that are taller than the page, so they must break across pages.</entry>
<entry name="arrange-block-at-top-fits.adoc" start="75379" lines="2204">Blocks placed at the top of a page that fit on that page and so must not break.</entry>
<entry name="arrange-block-below-top-does-not-fit.adoc" start="77585" lines="1032">Blocks starting below the top of a page that are taller than a full page, so they break.</entry>
<entry name="arrange-block-below-top-fits.adoc" start="78619" lines="2313">Blocks starting below the page top that fit on the page and should not be broken or moved.</entry>
<entry name="bare-theme.yml" start="80934" lines="1">Theme with an explicit null extends so no base theme is loaded.</entry>
<entry name="bmp.adoc" start="80937" lines="1">Embeds a BMP image to test the unsupported image format handling.</entry>
<entry name="book.adoc" start="80940" lines="7">Book doctype that includes two chapter files, for include and cross-file xref tests.</entry>
<entry name="box-drawing.adoc" start="80949" lines="19">Literal blocks containing Unicode box-drawing characters to test glyph rendering in monospace.</entry>
<entry name="broken.svg" start="80970" lines="1">Malformed SVG with an unclosed rect, used to test SVG parse errors.</entry>
<entry name="bundled-fonts-theme.yml" start="80973" lines="8">Theme that registers Noto Serif using bare font file names to test lookup in the bundled font directory.</entry>
<entry name="chronicles-abbreviated.adoc" start="80983" lines="48">Shortened chronicles book with TOC, index terms, section numbers and icons font for broad integration tests.</entry>
<entry name="color-like-value-theme.yml" start="81033" lines="2">Theme with an integer value (footer height 100) that could be mistaken for a hex color.</entry>
<entry name="custom-fonts-theme.yml" start="81037" lines="7">Theme extending default that merges an M+ 1p font from a relative path and sets it as the base font.</entry>
<entry name="custom-theme.yml" start="81046" lines="2">Minimal theme that only sets the base font family to Times-Roman.</entry>
<entry name="default-theme.yml" start="81050" lines="4">Custom theme named default (extends base, red base font) used to test theme name resolution versus the built-in default.</entry>
<entry name="diagrams.adoc" start="81056" lines="10">PlantUML sequence diagram block with a name attribute, for diagram extension handling.</entry>
<entry name="dry-run-block.adoc" start="81068" lines="5">Single warning admonition used for the dry-run conversion test.</entry>
<entry name="empty-theme.yml" start="81075" lines="0">Completely empty theme file.</entry>
<entry name="empty.adoc" start="81077" lines="0">Empty AsciiDoc document to test conversion with no content.</entry>
<entry name="equation.svg" start="81079" lines="114">Math equation SVG made of symbol glyphs, used to test symbol/use rendering.</entry>
<entry name="example-stamp.svg" start="81195" lines="3">Stamp-shaped path SVG with larger explicit width/height, used as a sample vector image.</entry>
<entry name="faulty.svg" start="81200" lines="1">SVG with an unknown element (foobar), used to test warnings for faulty SVG.</entry>
<entry name="fonts-theme.yml" start="81203" lines="15">Theme with a font catalog using YAML anchors, merge, fallbacks and an unresolved extends, using nonexistent font paths.</entry>
<entry name="footer-bg-letter.svg" start="81220" lines="4">Two-stripe SVG sized to a letter page width, used as a running footer background image.</entry>
<entry name="glyph-font-test.adoc" start="81226" lines="53">Arrows, dashes, symbols and scripts in normal and monospace text to test glyph and fallback font handling.</entry>
<entry name="gradient.svg" start="81281" lines="27">SVG with a linear gradient fill to test gradient support.</entry>
<entry name="green-bar-width.svg" start="81310" lines="45">Green badge SVG whose width and height attributes differ from viewBox, to test explicit sizing.</entry>
<entry name="green-bar.svg" start="81357" lines="45">Small green badge SVG with only a viewBox, used as an inline and running content image.</entry>
<entry name="header-bg-letter.svg" start="81404" lines="4">Two-stripe SVG sized to a letter page width, used as a running header background image.</entry>
<entry name="hello-with-custom-theme.adoc" start="81410" lines="3">Document that sets pdf-theme to custom via an attribute.</entry>
<entry name="hello.adoc" start="81415" lines="1">One-word document for basic conversion tests.</entry>
<entry name="hex-color-shorthand-theme.yml" start="81418" lines="16">Theme with unquoted hex colors, 3-digit shorthand, comments, variable references and nulls to test theme value parsing.</entry>
<entry name="i18n-font-test.adoc" start="81436" lines="170">Pangram-style document with diacritics and other scripts to check Noto Serif subset glyph coverage.</entry>
<entry name="interlaced-png.adoc" start="81608" lines="1">Embeds an interlaced PNG to test its handling.</entry>
<entry name="invalid-theme.yml" start="81611" lines="4">Theme with an invalid font catalog entry (a number instead of a path), to test error handling.</entry>
<entry name="lorem-ipsum.yml" start="81617" lines="29">Lorem ipsum text snippets of various lengths keyed by name, loaded by specs to generate filler content.</entry>
<entry name="ne.yml" start="81648" lines="4">Fake font-glyph data file with a version and a star character mapping, for the emoji/glyph lookup tests.</entry>
<entry name="nil-theme.yml" start="81654" lines="1">Theme file containing only a null document.</entry>
<entry name="otf-theme.yml" start="81657" lines="9">Theme extending default that registers an OpenType (.otf) font as the base font.</entry>
<entry name="page-background-image-theme.yml" start="81668" lines="3">Theme that sets a page background image.</entry>
<entry name="pdfmark-non-ascii-title.adoc" start="81673" lines="11">Book with a non-ASCII title and subject/keywords metadata to test PDF info encoding.</entry>
<entry name="red-blue-squares.svg" start="81686" lines="4">SVG of overlapping red and blue squares with inline-style fills and strokes.</entry>
<entry name="reference-to-self.adoc" start="81692" lines="12">Document with xrefs pointing to itself (with and without text) to test self-reference resolution.</entry>
<entry name="reference-to-sibling.adoc" start="81706" lines="6">Document with xrefs to a sibling document and its section, to test inter-document xrefs.</entry>
<entry name="running-footer-coerce-content-theme.yml" start="81714" lines="7">Theme with numeric and boolean footer content values, to test coercion to strings.</entry>
<entry name="running-header-outside-fixtures-theme.yml" start="81723" lines="8">Theme with a running header whose image path is relative to a parent directory, to test image path resolution.</entry>
<entry name="running-header-run-in-image-theme.yml" start="81733" lines="6">Theme with a running header that has an inline image followed by text in a single column.</entry>
<entry name="running-header-theme.yml" start="81741" lines="8">Theme with a three-column running header holding text and an SVG image in the center.</entry>
<entry name="secure.adoc" start="81751" lines="6">Book with a local image reference, used to test safe-mode restrictions on file access.</entry>
<entry name="square-100.svg" start="81759" lines="1">Square SVG with width and height of 100%.</entry>
<entry name="square-landscape.svg" start="81762" lines="1">Blue 100x100 square SVG for landscape page tests.</entry>
<entry name="square-portrait.svg" start="81765" lines="1">Red 100x100 square SVG for portrait page tests.</entry>
<entry name="square-viewbox-only.svg" start="81768" lines="1">Square SVG with a viewBox but no width or height.</entry>
<entry name="square.svg" start="81771" lines="1">Basic red 200x200 square SVG.</entry>
<entry name="svg-with-data-uri-image.svg" start="81774" lines="7">SVG embedding a PNG as a base64 data URI image.</entry>
<entry name="svg-with-data-uri-jpg-image.svg" start="81783" lines="7">SVG embedding a JPEG as a base64 data URI image.</entry>
<entry name="svg-with-data-uri-svg-image.svg" start="81792" lines="7">SVG embedding another SVG as a base64 data URI image.</entry>
<entry name="svg-with-generic-font.svg" start="81801" lines="5">SVG text using the generic font family serif.</entry>
<entry name="svg-with-gif-image.svg" start="81808" lines="3">SVG referencing a GIF image, an unsupported format inside SVG.</entry>
<entry name="svg-with-link.svg" start="81813" lines="7">SVG containing a hyperlink around text.</entry>
<entry name="svg-with-local-image.svg" start="81822" lines="4">SVG referencing a local PNG image by relative path.</entry>
<entry name="svg-with-local-svg.svg" start="81828" lines="5">SVG referencing another local SVG file.</entry>
<entry name="svg-with-missing-remote-image.svg" start="81835" lines="4">SVG referencing a remote image URL that does not exist.</entry>
<entry name="svg-with-non-url-image.svg" start="81841" lines="4">SVG referencing an image with a non-HTTP scheme (s3://).</entry>
<entry name="svg-with-text.svg" start="81847" lines="5">SVG text using the document font family M+ 1mn.</entry>
<entry name="svg-with-unknown-font.svg" start="81854" lines="5">SVG text using an unknown font family, falling back to the default SVG font.</entry>
<entry name="symbol-m.svg" start="81861" lines="17">Small SVG of the letter m built from glyph symbols, used for symbol handling.</entry>
<entry name="symbol-s.svg" start="81880" lines="17">Small SVG of the letter s built from glyph symbols, used for symbol handling.</entry>
<entry name="tab-indentation-theme.yml" start="81899" lines="4">Theme file indented with tab characters, to test tab handling in YAML.</entry>
<entry name="tall.svg" start="81905" lines="1">Green 200x600 tall SVG for page-fitting tests.</entry>
<entry name="TicTacToeGame.java" start="81908" lines="70" types="class TicTacToeGame; enum PLAYER">Java source file used as an include for source listing tests.</entry>
<entry name="tux-note.svg" start="81980" lines="21">Tux-style SVG icon used as a custom admonition icon.</entry>
<entry name="watermark.svg" start="82003" lines="9">Semi-transparent rotated DRAFT watermark SVG sized to an A4 page.</entry>
<entry name="wide.svg" start="82014" lines="1">Green 600x200 wide SVG for page-fitting tests.</entry>
<entry name="with-color.adoc" start="82017" lines="16">Document with a colored SVG image and a highlighted Ruby listing, to test color output.</entry>
</dir>
<dir path="asciidoctor-pdf/spec/fixtures/chapters" level="3">
<abstract>Multi-file book fixture with chapter includes and a nested chapter folder, used to test relative include and image paths across files.</abstract>
<entry name="chapter-1.adoc" start="82035" lines="4">Chapter fixture with an inter-document xref to chapter 2.</entry>
<entry name="chapter-2.adoc" start="82041" lines="10">Chapter fixture that includes a nested section file and xrefs to it.</entry>
</dir>
<dir path="asciidoctor-pdf/spec/fixtures/chapters/chapter-2" level="4">
<entry name="first-steps.adoc" start="82053" lines="3">Nested include fixture with a single subsection.</entry>
